WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
A chain of causes stretches
back through time.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.860
Thomas Aquinas argued it must
start with a first cause.

3
00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:12.680
Many arguments for God, and
against God, assume one creator:

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.220
all-powerful and all-good.

5
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.800
But Buddhism has no creator God.

6
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.920
Gods appear in many Buddhist stories, but
as beings within the cycle of rebirth,

7
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.730
not as its source.

8
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.420
So what happens to arguments for
God when a religion has no creator?

9
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.510
In this mission, you'll set Buddhist ideas
about ultimate reality beside Aquinas,

10
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.560
and see how they answer each other.

11
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.510
Then you'll test the Buddhist
teaching of no self against Descartes,

12
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.410
Hume and Parfit.

13
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:47.280
Your mission: find out what happens to
arguments for God when a religion has no

14
00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.120
creator.
